## When NOT to use it

A comparison page is most useful when it is honest
about what a feature does not do well. The polish pass
rewrites this section to name specific non-goals based
on the source — for now, the general rules:

- If your problem spans multiple features, prefer the
  orchestration layer above {{ title | lower }} to
  calling it directly.
- If you need behavior the public API does not expose,
  do not patch internals — file an issue or propose an
  extension point.
- If you are doing exploratory work, a throwaway
  script is usually better than wiring up
  {{ title | lower }} for a single use.

## Alternatives in this project

